{"authored" [{"question" "q-275796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "247103d5788deb0aa52b0d348f5e13c2a47b26635ae4d9517c2b3dfeedebdb99" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|-1\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot 2| \\\\  & =|5-8| \\\\  & =|-3| \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "247103d5788deb0aa52b0d348f5e13c2a47b26635ae4d9517c2b3dfeedebdb99" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275796" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2a8c1d86158d0bce6141f5941bd280e4068ea6f9a97c0ea498503a64bc1f8988" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275796" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "247103d5788deb0aa52b0d348f5e13c2a47b26635ae4d9517c2b3dfeedebdb99" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-275796" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "247103d5788deb0aa52b0d348f5e13c2a47b26635ae4d9517c2b3dfeedebdb99" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $T$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe area scale factor is\n{{field-1}} ." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "247103d5788deb0aa52b0d348f5e13c2a47b26635ae4d9517c2b3dfeedebdb99" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|8\\cdot 2-7\\cdot (-3)| \\\\  & =|16-(-21)| \\\\  & =37.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "247103d5788deb0aa52b0d348f5e13c2a47b26635ae4d9517c2b3dfeedebdb99" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316578" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2a8c1d86158d0bce6141f5941bd280e4068ea6f9a97c0ea498503a64bc1f8988" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316578" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "247103d5788deb0aa52b0d348f5e13c2a47b26635ae4d9517c2b3dfeedebdb99" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/455e0a08e2a0929a60d7fa1b76973e1b7a460efe8cc1cf01719ce211feacd8c0.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "247103d5788deb0aa52b0d348f5e13c2a47b26635ae4d9517c2b3dfeedebdb99" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 4=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2=-5.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-5\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "247103d5788deb0aa52b0d348f5e13c2a47b26635ae4d9517c2b3dfeedebdb99" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316591" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2a8c1d86158d0bce6141f5941bd280e4068ea6f9a97c0ea498503a64bc1f8988" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316591" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "247103d5788deb0aa52b0d348f5e13c2a47b26635ae4d9517c2b3dfeedebdb99" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-316591" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "30"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "247103d5788deb0aa52b0d348f5e13c2a47b26635ae4d9517c2b3dfeedebdb99" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85073" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A triangle $D$ has vertices $(-2,-1),(3,-1),(1,3).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "247103d5788deb0aa52b0d348f5e13c2a47b26635ae4d9517c2b3dfeedebdb99" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-85073" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/10c831c616279f443d10ed478a8b3b173d598da6e9b0b45edb7ecf487cf97f92.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 4=10.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 0=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,6\\,|\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/state.json" "file_sha256" "247103d5788deb0aa52b0d348f5e13c2a47b26635ae4d9517c2b3dfeedebdb99" "basis" 1045 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/ques