(T)=1\\cdot 0-3\\cdot (-2)=6.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,6\\,|\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fe0a83eb2a5714d714f1a7a8db4888a44e271d9be1db155a8f066616d3a9749"} {"question" "q-275983" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2eb5b5b5255b61e66349895901004514b914a96d1cda8b462887e3e3cb58b0b8"} {"question" "q-275983" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fe0a83eb2a5714d714f1a7a8db4888a44e271d9be1db155a8f066616d3a9749"} {"question" "q-275983" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "48"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/state.json" "file_sha256" "8fe0a83eb2a5714d714f1a7a8db4888a44e271d9be1db155a8f066616d3a9749"} {"question" "e-7454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/example-7454.json" "file_sha256" "33ce61ff3b3eff90b73d97587fc8ed27370ec5f6d5a6c71547fc1706adcf4d0f"} {"question" "e-7454" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|\\det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|2\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|8-3| \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/example-7454.json" "file_sha256" "33ce61ff3b3eff90b73d97587fc8ed27370ec5f6d5a6c71547fc1706adcf4d0f"} {"question" "e-5470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/e8ff769df4089e6ed9a47d56d7317acf41b8aef6a255abc705c0e7ec31a446ea.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/example-5470.json" "file_sha256" "c540f19593230c2bf66261e81290e2ad951b228377ba1f90d598d7a6d13d9518"} {"question" "e-5470" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\det(T) = 4 \\cdot 2 -  2 \\cdot (-1) = 10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,10\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/example-5470.json" "file_sha256" "c540f19593230c2bf66261e81290e2ad951b228377ba1f90d598d7a6d13d9518"} {"question" "e-5471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A triangle $D$ has vertices $(1,1)$, $(4,5),$ and $(-2,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/example-5471.json" "file_sha256" "e74b89bed562110da2e5613f76a220037b89e7198d5f1c29d7f0ad3d7279ef43"} {"question" "e-5471" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/ee8f0cf16983d87fa505303ed6372a3f389518d05b3e13f2e9e2121038792b84.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\det(T) = (-7) \\cdot 3 -  5 \\cdot (-2) = -11.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|-11|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/example-5471.json" "file_sha256" "e74b89bed562110da2e5613f76a220037b89e7198d5f1c29d7f0ad3d7279ef43"}] "usage" {"q-316578" [] "e-5471" [] "q-316607" [] "e-5470" [] "q-85073" [] "q-9294" 